  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through next Saturday)\nIssued at 350 PM EDT Sun Oct 4 2026\n\nThe warm temperatures will begin to moderate as the additional cloud \ncover with the approaching boundary allow a cooling trend of a few \ndegrees per day to emerge for Tuesday and then Wednesday. Regardless \nif an area of low pressure does indeed develop along the boundary \nearly in the week somewhere around north or north central Florida, \nthis week does appear to feature unsettled weather for the South \nFlorida forecast. A change in this forecast cycle from previous \nguidance is the insistence of reinforcing shortwave troughs at the \nmid levels to keep the front stalled a bit further south than \npreviously forecast. Obviously this is one model cycle but that is \nsomething that will also need to be monitored as the repetitive \nbouts of rainfall that could emerge could be problematic for any \nareas that become saturated.",
